          "text": "Went to Google's Genesis2Genesis conference today! Awesome speakers (including Dave Rensin for the keynote) and talking to people between sessions.\n\nA few things I took away:\n- Agents are changing how a lot of work gets done, including in roles that aren't engineering. All sorts of financial work can be automated if done right.\n- At a company like Google that rollout is well underway. My own read is that small and mid-sized businesses still have a lot of ground to cover before they're at the same level. This is probably one of the biggest opportunities of the next decade.\n- Nobody's career path was linear. A few of the speakers ended up where they are through opportunities they didn't plan for.\n\nIt's a huge team, but the culture came across as genuinely collaborative. I'm glad to have met a lot of interesting people and got a much better sense of where AI and finance are heading.\n\nThanks to Shayla McLin Green as well as all the Googlers who helped make this event possible!\n\n#G2GBAYAREA2026",
          "type": "post",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alan-tai-nu_g2gbayarea2026-activity-7494253699486072833-PW5k"
