            "shareUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alan-tai-nu_the-us-government-just-handed-anthropic-the-activity-7473517334754713600-miXC",
            "showContributionExperience": false,
            "showSocialDetail": true
          },
          "text": "The US government just handed Anthropic the best marketing it could ask for, by banning their product.\n\nLast Friday, Fable 5 and Mythos 5, Anthropic's most powerful models, went dark. Not a bug. A federal directive. As far as I can tell, it's the first time a deployed AI model has been pulled offline because the government decided it was too capable to leave running.\n\nThink about what that actually signals.\n\nEvery other lab spends millions trying to convince people their model is the most powerful one out there. Anthropic just got the US government to say it for them, for free.\n\nAnd the name writes the rest. The family is literally called Mythos. When access comes back, and it will, it doesn't return as just another model. It returns with a story: forbidden, then restored. People line up for that.\n\nScarcity didn't kill the demand here. It built the myth.",
          "type": "post",
          "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alan-tai-nu_the-us-government-just-handed-anthropic-the-activity-7473517334754713600-miXC"
        },
